   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 6,
   "t": 78.5,
   "fen": "rnbqkb1r/ppp2ppp/4pn2/3p4/2PP4/2N5/PP2PPPP/R1BQKBNR w KQkq - 2 4",
   "line": [
    "Nf6"
   ],
   "spoken": "This is the QGD, the opening to recommend to every beginner — a gateway to so much else."
  },
  {
   "ply": 7,
   "t": 81.5,
   "fen": "rnbqkb1r/ppp2ppp/4pn2/3p2B1/2PP4/2N5/PP2PPPP/R2QKBNR b KQkq - 3 4",
   "line": [
    "Bg5"
   ],
   "spoken": "White pins with the bishop to g5. The traditional reply is the bishop to e7, but for a little edge there is the knight to d7 — which looks like it just drops a pawn."
  },
  {
   "ply": 8,
   "t": 97,
   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/pppn1ppp/4pn2/3p2B1/2PP4/2N5/PP2PPPP/R2QKBNR w KQkq - 4 5",
   "line": [
    "Nbd7"
   ],
   "spoken": "And there it is, the knight to d7 — inviting a very old, very famous trap."
  },
  {
   "ply": 9,
   "t": 99.5,
   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/pppn1ppp/4pn2/3p2B1/2PP4/2N1P3/PP3PPP/R2QKBNR b KQkq - 0 5",
   "line": [
    "e3"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 8,
   "t": 101,
   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/pppn1ppp/4pn2/3p2B1/2PP4/2N5/PP2PPPP/R2QKBNR w KQkq - 4 5",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 9,
   "t": 119,
   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/pppn1ppp/4pn2/3p2B1/2PP4/2N1P3/PP3PPP/R2QKBNR b KQkq - 0 5",
   "line": [
    "e3"
   ],
   "spoken": "White plays the main move e3. And Black develops the bishop to e7 — not d6 — mainly to break the pin, since White was threatening to win a pawn.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 10,
   "t": 132,
   "fen": "r1bqk2r/pppnbppp/4pn2/3p2B1/2PP4/2N1P3/PP3PPP/R2QKBNR w KQkq - 1 6",
   "line": [
    "Be7"
   ],
   "spoken": "The bishop comes to e7, unpinning."
  },
  {
   "ply": 11,
   "t": 135,
   "fen": "r1bqk2r/pppnbppp/4pn2/3p2B1/2PP4/2N1PN2/PP3PPP/R2QKB1R b KQkq - 2 6",
   "line": [
    "Nf3"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 12,
   "t": 140,
   "fen": "r1bq1rk1/pppnbppp/4pn2/3p2B1/2PP4/2N1PN2/PP3PPP/R2QKB1R w KQ - 3 7",
   "line": [
    "O-O"
   ],
   "spoken": "Black completes the kingside — castling short."
  },
  {
   "ply": 13,
   "t": 147,
   "fen": "r1bq1rk1/pppnbppp/4pn2/3p2B1/2PP4/2N1PN2/PP3PPP/2RQKB1R b K - 4 7",
   "line": [
    "Rc1"
   ],
   "spoken": "Now the question is what to do with this bishop. This is the Capablanca simplifying system — a way of playing the QGD that has been around since the 1800s."
  },
  {
   "ply": 14,
   "t": 186.5,
   "fen": "r1bq1rk1/pp1nbppp/2p1pn2/3p2B1/2PP4/2N1PN2/PP3PPP/2RQKB1R w K - 0 8",
   "line": [
    "c6"
   ],
   "spoken": "The move is c6 — and be warned, it looks bad, it looks passive. But it is the heart of the system."
  },
  {
   "ply": 15,
   "t": 195,
   "fen": "r1bq1rk1/pp1nbppp/2p1pn2/3p2B1/2PP4/2NBPN2/PP3PPP/2RQK2R b K - 1 8",
   "line": [
    "Bd3"
   ],
   "spoken": "White develops the bishop to d3. Yes, c6 does hem in Black's own light bishop for now."
  },
  {
   "ply": 16,
   "t": 207,
   "fen": "r1bq1rk1/pp1nbppp/2p1pn2/6B1/2pP4/2NBPN2/PP3PPP/2RQK2R w K - 0 9",
   "line": [
    "dxc4"
   ],
   "spoken": "Now something even more paradoxical — the capture on c4. Notice Black waited for White to commit that bishop first, so taking now wins a tempo."
  },
  {
   "ply": 13,
   "t": 209,
   "fen": "r1bq1rk1/pppnbppp/4pn2/3p2B1/2PP4/2N1PN2/PP3PPP/2RQKB1R b K - 4 7",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 16,
   "t": 210.5,
   "fen": "r1bq1rk1/pp1nbppp/2p1pn2/6B1/2BP4/2N1PN2/PP3PPP/2RQK2R w K - 0 9",
   "line": [
